{"Test docstring contradicts the assertion - docstring states errors don't block offset commits for other messages, but assertion checks that no commits happened, when actually both offsets should be committed due to the finally block always calling complete_offset": 0.7064523696899414, "Using `assert` for runtime validation is unsafe because assertions are disabled when Python runs with the `-O` (optimize) flag, causing silent failures and unclear AttributeError instead of clear error messages": 0.349622517824173, "`queue.ShutDown` was introduced in Python 3.13 and will raise AttributeError at runtime if targeting Python 3.11 or 3.12 - need to verify minimum supported Python version or add compatibility shim": 0.8630988001823425, "`q.shutdown(immediate=False)` on line 238 has the same Python 3.13 compatibility issue as queue.ShutDown": 0.9258544445037842, "`join` method calls `close()` which causes the queue pool to be shut down twice and `commit_thread.join()` to be called again when arroyo framework calls both close() and join()": 0.7235016226768494, "`join` method semantically should only wait for in-flight work to complete, not initiate shutdown - should be implemented to wait for queue pool to drain rather than delegating to close()": 0.688541829586029}